od  what makes falsehood so necessary is our  proclivity for making unfortunate  associations it is in theory of course  in  tirely possible to love someone beat li  and at the same time to believe that  they are terrible at baking but in our  own minds the rejection of our cakes  tends to feel synonymous with the  rejection of our being with forcing any  half-decent person to lie to us by the  abducens of our thought processes it is  because the aunt is in the grip of a  falsehood if you don't like my cake you  can't like me that we will have to offer  her a dose of untruth  I like your cake by which we can make  sure that a big truth I like you can  remain safe the same principle applies  in more tricky situations suppose a  woman goes away to a conference one  night after a lovely conversation in the  bar she gets carried away and slips into  bed with an international colleague they  don't make love but they do have a sweet  time they rub their lips together and  entwine their legs they will almost  certainly never see one another again  it wasn't an attempt to start a  long-term relationship and it meant very  little when the woman gets home her  partner asks her how her evening was she  says she watched CNN and ordered a club  sandwich in her room on her own she lies  because she knows her partner well and  can predict how he would respond to the  truth he would be wounded to the call  would be convinced that his wife didn't  love him and would probably conclude the  divorce was the only option but this  assessment of the truth would not be  true in reality it is of course  eminently possible to love someone  deeply and every so often go to bed with  another person and yet kind people  understand the entrenched and socially  endorsed associations between infidelity  and callousness so almost all of us the  news I spent a night with a colleague  from the Singapore office which is true  has to end up meaning I don't love you  anymore which is not true at all and 